Z||000000||Carrolles||01-23-2000||03:30 PM||||Cliff,<P>I installed PIP and am trying to post a picture.  I hit browse and choose a picture.  When I click on Post It it opens the window saying it is uploading but it never gets off zero.  If I hit cancel nothing happens.  I have to ctrl-alt-del to get the not-responding message to end task.  I am running IE 4.0.  Any ideas?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||01-23-2000||04:06 PM||||To be honest, I've no idea what could be wrong. For most people it seems to work fine but some are having similar problems. It could be that you're behind a firewall or something. Are you using AOL by any chance?<P>Next time you try it, let it run in the background for about 5 minutes - it should time out eventually (it's a bug in the Windows library that it takes so long to time out). The cancel button not doing anything is a known bug in the program (actually, it's not a bug, I just forgot to implement it...).<P>In the mean time I'll try to find out what happens if you run PIP behind a firewall.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-23-2000||04:24 PM||||Cliff,<P>I am running it on a network connection at my office.  That may be the problem.<P>Thanks for your help.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-24-2000||01:46 AM||||I had a similar problem trying to run it at work. I assumed it was the firewall but never found out for sure. <P>Cliff, does the program attempt to use a firewall if there is one ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-24-2000||12:36 PM||||No it doesn't, it always assumes direct connection to the internet. I need to find a way to set up a firewall on my end so I can test it and create changes if necessary...<BR>||||reg||1
